lines=['# BangaLangin foundational calibration refinement','',f'Offline review · {datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat()}','', '## Recommendation','', '**Continue offline foundational research. Do not implement this model in the live Trade Analyzer, proceed to Phase2, or begin the full roster optimizer.** This pass delivers exact QA3/category math, historical game evidence, an expanded prospect experiment and a reproducible checkpoint. It does not deliver a validated common dynasty-value scale. Pitcher prospect labels still inherit the Phase1 reduced-category scale; rare upper-tail estimates remain underidentified.','', 'The production formula and player data were not edited. Main remains `cba5e8095a91e9ef5c3fe776ec9d7d78b8005013`. This checkpoint builds on Phase1 `f80d9b5355ce370f76987d65e6aee29d4a1787dc`, which in turn preserves U2.','', '## Evidence gained and what it does not establish','', '| Finding | Interpretation |','|---|---|','| Exact QA3 differs materially from QS | Conventional QS is an invalid substitution for this league. |','| Weekly eligibility materially changes SP marginal contribution | No universal SP anchor can represent owners near and far from35IP. |','| Expanded baseline beats U2 rank prior on2020 validation | Supports this specific five-year outcome prediction experiment, not the complete U2 trade architecture or every horizon. |','| Improvement over saved Phase1 is uncertain | Do not claim the expanded baseline is statistically proven superior to Phase1. |','| Five-year development superstars remain2 | More ranking rows did not solve upper-tail identification. |','| Seven-year development superstars rise to8 | Delayed maturation matters; these are separate diagnostics, not replacement training labels. |','| FV/tools/trajectory/MiLB features fail to show improvement | Keep simple baseline; this does not prove scouting lacks predictive value generally. |','', '## Frozen methodology and chronology','',f'Original protocol frozen at `{json.load(open(P/"protocol.json"))["frozen_at_utc"]}`. Final model/scaler/identity receipt saved at `{freeze["frozen_before_final_labels_utc"]}` before the code obtains2020 labels. See `protocol.json` and `results/trained-model-freeze.json`.','', 'The primary outcome definition remains five calendar years, evaluation year through year+4. A regular has at least two seasons with250AB or40IP. Peak is the mean of the two highest actual annual Phase1 intrinsic scores. Above-average/star/superstar thresholds remain6.82833342604977 /11.615250774606945 /17.59838994663511. Missing seasons contribute zero. Actual2020 counts are retained, never annualized. These labels are realized fantasy-production proxies, not scouting truths and not career-bust judgments. They omit QA3 and retain pooled pitcher/hitter scaling limitations.','', 'Primary development has one first-observed record per ID from dated preseason rankings through2015. Its labels end by2019, before the2020 evaluation.2020 prospects with any development identity are excluded; all100 remain.2017/2018 were already exposed in Phase1 and are not claimed as untouched confirmation.2019 rankings provide trajectory only.2021 rankings are reserved and neither fitted nor evaluated.2020 has now been evaluated once in this pass and cannot be used as an untouched holdout again.','', 'Pre-final addendum: first-occurrence2015 records lacked all five classes; matched scouting experiments instead use all100 unique2015 identities, still entirely inside development. Even this cohort has no five-year superstars. Those models predict zero for the absent class and cannot calibrate superstar probabilities. This limitation is explicit in the freeze receipt. No feature was selected for best final score.','', 'Baseline: training-only standardized log(rank), DOB-based evaluation age and hitter/pitcher role; multinomial L2 logistic C=.3. Separate fixed feature experiments add prior-year MiLB K%, BB%, ISO/ERA and workload; FV; future tools; or prior ranking trajectory.2015 matched core/FV/tools/trajectory comparisons use identical100 training and100 test IDs.2015 and2020 each have100 grade/tool profiles; these experiments do not infer grades for older cohorts. Hitting tools are Hit/GamePower/Run or Speed; pitching tools are Fastball/best Slider or Curveball/Command or Control. `+` is represented by+2.5, an exploratory harmonization assumption.','', 'Prior MiLB performance is not level-, park-, era- or league-adjusted. Dated development level and systematic injury coverage were insufficient for matched experiments; neither is presented as tested. There is no assumption that additional features help. The saved Phase1 rank/role probabilities are reproduced using its saved coefficients and intercept differences recovered from stored predictions, checked to1e-8; Phase1 was not refitted.','', '## Historical coverage and source-date audit','',f'600 new primary FanGraphs top 100 observations across2010/2011/2014/2015/2019/2020.680 records were extracted including80 below rank100; only top 100 enter calibration. Combined with the399 inherited MLB ranking observations, the coverage inventory has999 primary observations. The training slice uses the two inherited2012/2013 cohorts, not the exposed2017/2018 outcomes. All680 extracted records resolve to stable MLBAM IDs using explicit aliases/overrides and DOB plausibility; no identity was chosen to match a favorable outcome. Manual alias/override review is preserved in `identities.py`; historical team/name source evidence is not independently certified for every override.','',f'Development: **{p["coverage"]["development_unique"]} distinct players**, class counts **{p["coverage"]["development_counts"]}**. Final2020: **{p["coverage"]["final_unique"]} distinct players**, counts **{p["coverage"]["final_counts"]}**.13 final-cohort players had some2019 MLB production, so this is not exclusively pre-debut prediction. First-observed development rank is not always the same career evaluation stage as the final cohort; this population shift limits transportability.','', '22,000 approximately primary-role MLB player-seasons (exact21,973) across2010–2025; new2024/2025 seasons append to the preserved2010–2023 checkpoint. Two-way players are reduced to a primary production role; this does not solve Fantrax two-way asset eligibility. MiLB source seasons2009–2014 and2019 are prior-year features. API totalSplits is inconsistent across multi-sport responses; returned arrays are preserved and deduplicated by player/team/league, with no duplicates detected. The query limit is100,000, but completeness of minor archives cannot be guaranteed solely by the API metadata.','', '| Ranking source | Verified article date | Use |','|---|---|---|']
