lines += ['', 'The new FanGraphs headers predate their MLB seasons. Original article dates are not the current website footer date. Historical retrieval is not independent archive proof of unedited grades. The inherited MLB2012/2013 lists explicitly describe preseason rankings but are republished archives; their original publication days remain unverified. March1 is an age-computation approximation, not publication evidence. Full independently verified historical timestamps remain a limitation. Current stable DOB/IDs are used only for identity and age; current status and later evaluations are not training features.','', '## Exact QA3 and weekly category engine','', 'A player-game appearance qualifies if `(outs>=15 and ER<=2) or (outs>=18 and ER<=3)`.5.2IP is17outs and fails the second branch;5IP/2ER qualifies and5IP/3ER does not. Supplied QA3 definition does not require a starter flag; qualifying bulk relief appearances therefore count. Conventional QS is separately counted only for starts with>=18outs and<=3ER.','',f'Retrosheet supplies **{sum(r["pitcher_appearances"] for r in q["coverage"]):,} regular-season pitcher appearances**,2010–2025. Across these seasons: **{sum(r["QA3"] for r in q["coverage"]):,} QA3**, versus **{sum(r["conventional_QS"] for r in q["coverage"]):,} QS**.','', '| Year | QA3 | Conventional QS | Difference | Qualifying nonstarter appearances |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in q['coverage'][-3:]:lines.append(f'| {r["year"]} | {r["QA3"]} | {r["conventional_QS"]} | {r["additional_QA3"]} | {r["QA3_nonstarters"]} |')
lines += ['', 'All12 equal-weight categories are implemented from raw component totals: hitters HR/R/RBI/SB/AVG/OPS; pitchers ER(lower), K,3SV+2HLD,QA3,K/BB with inherited zero-walk adjustment1.01K,WHIP. ER is raw earned runs, **not ERA**. AVG/OPS/KBB/WHIP are recalculated on combined team totals, not averaged player ratios.35IP per7days is an eligibility gate; failing loses all six pitching categories. Period-length proration is implemented. All-star and other nonstandard Fantrax scoring calendars are not reconstructed; comparisons use hypothetical full Monday–Sunday periods. Zero-exposure hitting-ratio edge cases are not independently verified against Fantrax. Final MLB/Retrosheet corrections may differ from the league’s168-hour correction freeze.','', 'Official MLB weekly pitching totals provide holds absent from Retrosheet.162 weekly responses cover2010/2011/2012/2018/2023/2024. Retrosheet and MLB reconcile exactly across63,027 week/player pairs for outs,ER,K,BB,H andSV: **zero discrepancies**, no unmatched Retrosheet IDs and no duplicate weekly player rows. QA3 comes from the independent game calculation. Boundary, baseball-innings notation, ratio aggregation, raw-ER direction, zero-walk and minimum/proration checks pass. Ten damaged compressed cache files were detected and refreshed; replacements use validated atomic writes. This was input repair, not a restart of Phase1.','', 'The information used here was obtained free of charge from and is copyrighted by Retrosheet. Interested parties may contact Retrosheet at 20 Sunset Rd., Newark, DE 19711. Primary sources: [Retrosheet downloads](https://www.retrosheet.org/downloads/csvdownloads.html), [field definitions](https://www.retrosheet.org/downloads/csvcontents.html), [MLB StatsAPI](https://statsapi.mlb.com/api/v1/stats), [Chadwick identity register](https://github.com/chadwickbureau/register).','', '## Hitter/SP/RP contribution diagnostics','', '40 fixed hypothetical roster contexts per year2018/2024 are selected from qualified prior-year pools using seed3505. Each has13H and9P=22active: C/1B/2B/3B/SS/CI/MI/5OF/UT, plus6SP/3RP occupying generic P slots. Historical fielding-game counts enforce previous-season20-game eligibility or the most-played fallback. Candidate hitters use UT; SP and RP replace their corresponding ninth pitching slot. Contexts with the candidate already on either side are excluded, preventing duplicate identities. No weekly best-player selection or optimizer is used. Opponent contexts are fixed as well.','', 'Two distinct outputs are saved: marginal category points versus a zero-output occupied slot, and signed replacement delta versus a fixed prior-year-selected same-role player. Zero-output is a hypothetical injured/nonplaying slot, not verified obtainable replacement. Replacement players are not claimed to be current unowned Fantrax alternatives. The counts, roster assignments and contexts are saved. No positional-scarcity bonus or acquisition premium is added.','', 'These unmanaged fixed rosters often miss35IP because their players lose playing time or are injured. This deliberately exposes eligibility sensitivity, but makes them unsuitable as a realistic forecast of active owners who rotate reserves. Missing weeks count as zero rather than giving injured players fictitious innings.','', '|2024 player | Role | Marginal points/week, all contexts | Gate disabled diagnostic | Both backgrounds eligible | Signed replacement delta, qualified contexts |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in c:lines.append(f'| {r["name"]} | {r["role"]} | {sum(r["all_context_marginal"]):.3f} | {sum(r["eligibility_gate_disabled_marginal"]):.3f} | {sum(r["conditional_marginal"]):.3f} | {r["conditional_replacement_delta"]:.3f} |')
lines += ['', 'Gate-disabled values are a diagnostic counterfactual, not a league-rule change. Qualified-context results condition on observed background and opponent reaching35IP before candidate contribution; that selection is not causal or predictive. Wheeler/Skubal benefit strongly in deficient contexts; their apparent scale changes considerably in qualified contexts. Gausman’s qualified-context replacement delta is negative despite a positive marginal contribution, demonstrating why intrinsic contribution and replacement surplus must remain separate. Hitter/SP/RP values were never adjusted to equalize medians.','', 'The old Phase1 SP30th-percentile intrinsic anchor was−0.564 and SP60th-percentile surplus anchor−0.484; a near-zero/clipped regular value can emerge from the reduced pitching vector and replacement subtraction. Exact QA3 and eligibility reveal omitted contribution mechanisms. However, the new weekly context units are **not yet a validated forecast distribution**, and have not replaced the primary prospect labels. This pass diagnoses the pitching anchor; it does not certify its resolution in an integrated dynasty model. The saved Phase1 aging/workload/residual model remains preserved; new weekly aging, injury/durability forecasts and owner horizons require validation before category-point paths can feed utility.','', '## Out-of-sample prospect results','', 'Lower Brier/log loss is better. Every model below is evaluated on the same1002020 prospects, outcomes through2024.','', '| Model | Multiclass Brier | Log loss | Superstar Brier |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for k,r in p['metrics'].items():lines.append(f'| {k} | {r["multiclass_brier"]:.4f} | {r["log_loss"]:.4f} | {r["superstar_brier"]:.4f} |')
