for k,r in p['paired_comparisons'].items():lines.append(f'| {k} | {r["mean_brier_difference"]:.4f} | [{r["paired_95_interval"][0]:.4f}, {r["paired_95_interval"][1]:.4f}] |')
lines += ['', 'The expanded core improves over U2’s generic rank prior on this outcome test. Its improvement over saved Phase1 is not statistically clear. Added MiLB/FV/trajectory features do not show a gain; the tool addition worsens this specific matched test. Do not interpret these results as a contest proving the whole unified architecture, feature causality, or production trade validity. Matched2015 models have no superstar training case: their zero superstar probabilities are an estimator failure of coverage, not evidence that prospects have zero superstar chance. Final validation has Bobby Witt Jr. as its only five-year superclass; Luis Robert, Julio Rodriguez, Nico Hoerner and Corbin Carroll meet the frozen star class. No trade outcome is used as a target.','', '## Upper-tail uncertainty, delayed arrival and career completion','', f'500 identity-level development bootstrap draws were attempted;{p["bootstrap_successful"]} all-class fits succeeded and{p["bootstrap_missing_class_exclusions"]} were excluded for missing classes.90% model probability intervals are saved, but condition on successful fits and fixed definitions/sources. They are not comprehensive uncertainty bounds; with two training superstars they can look misleadingly narrow. Empirical Wilson95% and Jeffreys95% bin ranges are therefore also supplied, including zero-event upper bounds.','', 'For development top 10 hitters, five-year superclass frequency is0/12 with Wilson95% range0–24.3%; the seven-year diagnostic is1/12 with range1.5–35.4%. Top 10 pitchers have0/6, Wilson upper bound39.0%, not a justified zero probability. These bins are small first-observed samples, not precision estimates for individual elite prospects. The rank5 age19 logistic superclass point estimates (~0.64%H/~0.33%P) should **not** be operationalized as reliable probabilities. Their narrow conditional bootstrap bands do not override the wide empirical uncertainty.','', 'Across359 development IDs, seven-year class counts are[124,118,70,39,8], compared with five-year[157,114,54,32,2].33 minimal contributors become contributors;13 cross into star/superstar. The extra six superclass cases include Harper/Arenado/Yelich/Story/Devers/Judge. This is a strong warning against equating a five-year minimal label with a lifetime bust. Seven-year outcomes ending after the2020 evaluation are not used to train2020 values. They remain a separate retrospective diagnostic.2020 seven-year outcomes end in2026 and are incomplete as of the2025 outcome cutoff; no seven-year final evaluation is fabricated.','', 'Observed-through2025 and five-/seven-year outcomes are separate from complete career outcomes. No player is declared to have a complete career merely because he has not appeared recently. Retirement/death completion evidence has not been systematically verified, so this checkpoint does not present a complete-career cohort or use incomplete careers as career busts. Expansion materially increases regular/above-average/star samples but **does not resolve five-year superstar calibration**.','', '## Unified architecture and comparison stress tests','', 'The four ledgers remain distinct: (1) intrinsic future fantasy-contribution distribution; (2) replacement difficulty measured against realistic alternatives; (3) acquisition scarcity/market cost; (4) owner utility using a horizon and only incremental legal roster opportunities. The category engine supplies context-conditioned contribution observations, not market value. No acquisition scarcity is inferred from prospect outcome class. No replacement, superstar or capacity bonus is added twice.','', 'An offline contract in `ledger_contract.py` evaluates E[U(contribution)] once per asset/outcome, then sums asset expectations with inherited Contender65/25/10, Balanced40/30/30, Rebuild15/25/60 three-year weights. Nonlinear utility curvature.04 and its threshold remain **assumptions in old score units**, not newly fitted category-point preferences. Unique opportunity IDs reject duplicate capacity credit. Capacity is accepted only as a supplied joint before/after incremental result; a full optimizer was not built. There is no standalone consolidation bonus and no U(package total) superstar amplification.','', 'Elite/mid MLB hitter/SP/RP comparisons are supplied in weekly diagnostics. Elite hitting/pitching prospects and top5-versus-multiple lower-ranked packages are supplied as frozen-label intrinsic utility sensitivities, not validated trade values. For age19 rank5H, expected peak utility9.09 versus two rank25H10.75 and ranks25+50+90H11.54; analogous P5.32 versus5.93 and6.60. These packages require more roster opportunities; no fabricated space/scarcity adjustment is added to force the elite asset ahead. A sensitivity coefficient cannot be used to tune these outcomes toward a preferred trade verdict.','', 'Young MLB stars versus elite prospects cannot yet be defensibly valued on the same calibrated future category paths: the new weekly context values and old prospect peak labels are incompatible units/horizons. Synthetic immediate-versus-delayed paths demonstrate owner-horizon behavior in `ledger-and-narrative-checks.json`, explicitly not real player forecasts. This comparison is an identified integration weakness, not a silently completed test.','', 'Josuar, De Vries, Acuña and Guerrero remain preserved U2/Phase1 stress evidence; they were not refitted or tuned to equality. Their historical evaluation-date feature crosswalks, complete category-path forecasts, current ownership and pick outcomes are insufficient for a defensible new numeric rescoring. Existing U2 comparisons remain valid as saved experiments, not as calibrated endorsements. THEN uses only trade-date evidence; NOW uses current evidence; REALIZED SO FAR reports observed production separately. No completed trade is assumed fair and later realized outcomes do not train its THEN value.','', '## Requested trade explanation blurb','', 'The offline renderer creates a separate explanation for each owner using that owner’s strategy, sent/received values, uncertainty and specific drivers. Positive changes say benefits; small negative changes say slightly worse off; an interval crossing zero says uncertain. It does not choose a winner because an asset is an elite prospect. Values and direction are read from model output, not hard-coded.','']
for s in load('trade-explanation-examples.json')['owner_explanations']:lines += ['> '+s,'']
lines += ['These two examples deliberately use **saved U2** numbers, not the new calibrated verdict. They preserve the roughly-neutral Shea Contender / negative Sandlot Rebuild result instead of inventing a different answer. The wording renderer and implementation specification are ready for review; nothing has been activated in production. A future live blurb should name the assets, separate immediate category production from future upside, show missing evidence and uncertainty, and describe each owner independently.','', '## League constraints and deferred work','', 'User correction overrides the older17-round attachment: **20rounds total; Rounds1–5FYPD are the only tradable picks; Rounds6–20 are free-agent acquisition access and never standalone assets.** No assumption of15 usable openings per owner. Actual63total excludingIR,22active,11reserve,30minors,8IR; minor eligibility≤503careerAB/162IP. Daily substitutions, IR enforcement, current openings, FYPD obligations and availability/verified Fantrax ownership are not reconciled by this fixed-roster experiment. No Phase2 collection, draft-pick recalibration or roster optimizer has begun.','', '## Smallest defensible next foundational stage, subject to review','', '1. Freeze a new shared outcome scale derived from exact league category production and realistic weekly backgrounds. Validate forecasts of workload, age/aging, absence, injury and starter/reliever role before using those paths for both MLB and prospects. Do not relabel2020 and claim a fresh holdout.','2. Predefine a time-to-arrival/maturation outcome or censored longitudinal likelihood; preserve five-year outcomes separately. Obtain older, independently dated cohorts so longer observation windows can mature before an evaluation date. Validate complete-career status separately.','3. Add enough independent star/superstar cases to support tail estimates; prioritize verified older FV/tool archives and level-/era-adjusted MiLB evidence. Fit only pre-evaluation features. Rank trajectories should use clustered player identities and comparable evaluation stages, not inflate sample size with repeated stars.','4. Reserve2021 for a final frozen test. Until additional untouched datasets exist, do not repeatedly optimize against the now-exposed2020 cohort. Report both absolute probability calibration and role/rank subgroup uncertainty.','5. Only after category paths and upper tails are validated, compare real young MLB assets with elite prospects and re-score dated historical stress cases with THEN/NOW/REALIZED kept separate. Proceed to league-specific replacement/availability and joint capacity optimization only with further approval.','', '## Reproducibility and preservation','', 'See README.md, requirements.txt, protocol.json, input-source-manifest.json, input replay archive and results. Existing Phase1/U2 code and results were read without refitting them. Collectors save raw source snapshots; compact replay inputs preserve the exact analyzed selected data. Full Retrosheet/source ZIPs remain in this workspace, with source hashes recorded; they are excluded from Git to avoid duplicating large public archives. Missing full archive collection can be reproduced separately, but is not necessary to replay calibration diagnostics.','', 'The successor research branch includes only this isolated research package and a branch-specific `vercel.json` deployment-disabled rule. Production/main configuration remains unchanged. Read-only hosting inspection found that the prior Phase1 research commit had generated an automatic preview despite skip markers; those markers are not relied on for this checkpoint. No merge, live Trade Analyzer change or deploy command is authorized or performed.','']
